# Web presentation

Read `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md` and the relevant `docs/design/` documents.

- Svelte owns menus, HUD, overlays and application shell.
- PixiJS owns the game table, cards, spatial effects and primary gameplay animation.
- Do not implement the table as a collection of ordinary HTML card divs.
- UI talks to `GameSession`; do not duplicate card legality/winner/scoring logic in Svelte or Pixi.
- Sprites reflect game state. Sprite position is never authoritative state.
- Maintain a presentation/animation queue driven by emitted game events.
- Lock input only for presentation sequencing when needed; do not confuse this with gameplay legality.
- Keep illegal-by-rule cards clickable so Palito remains possible.
- Mouse and touch must both work for necessary interactions.
- Desktop-first, but preserve usable responsive behavior.
- Clean up Pixi resources/listeners when leaving or restarting a game.
